  "claim": "A drama club has hosted matches at stadium, where Robin Dutt started coaching in the 2011–12 season, since 1958. This club has Willibert Kremer as a scout.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Bayer 04 Leverkusen. Sentence: The club plays in the Bundesliga, the top tier of the German football league system, and hosts matches at the BayArena.\nPage: BayArena. Sentence: BayArena (] ) is a football stadium in Leverkusen, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, which has been the home ground of Bundesliga club Bayer Leverkusen since 1958.\nPage: Willibert Kremer. Sentence: Willibert Kremer (born 15 October 1939 in Hochneukirch) is a German football coach and a former player who currently works as a scout with Bayer 04 Leverkusen.\nPage: Robin Dutt. Sentence: Starting from the 2011–12 season, he signed a two-year managerial contract with Bayer Leverkusen after the previous manager Jupp Heynckes confirmed on 21 March 2011 that he would not be extending his stay at the BayArena.",
